  "worked_solution": "Notice that the given matrix is diagonal.\n\nThe inverse of a diagonal matrix can be found as follows: \n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & 0 & \u22ef & 0 \\\\ 0 & {a}_{22} & \u22ef & 0 \\\\ \u22ee & \u22ee & \u22f1 & \u22ee \\\\ 0 & 0 & \u22ef & {a}_{nn}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{a}_{11}} & 0 & \u22ef & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{{a}_{22}} & \u22ef & 0 \\\\ \u22ee & \u22ee & \u22f1 & \u22ee \\\\ 0 & 0 & \u22ef & \\frac{1}{{a}_{nn}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
